graph LR
    B1["B.1 Doraiath"] --- B4["B.4 Nuthora"]
    B2["B.2 Immora"] --- B5["B.5 Naugfast"]
    B3["B.3 Ghutrrun"] -.- B6["B.6 Kkithik"]
    B2 --- C1["C.1 Immorael"]
    B5 --- C20["C.20 Nessekirel"]
```

A forest of trees, per `patterns/region/Wild.md`. The three Landmarks - Doraiath, Immora
and Ghutrrun - do not interconnect: a party roams Lindmarn and finds them, and depth
happens below a Landmark rather than between them. Each of the three carries a child, which
is how this region carries weight. B.4 and B.5 are Hidden and hang off their parent by a
normal edge, reached through a visible detail at the parent. B.6 is Secret and hangs off
Ghutrrun by a hidden edge, reachable only through the Clue/Trigger/Payload written into
that Landmark. Two edges leave the region for C: the stair at Immora, and the drowned
breach below Naugfast.
